%N A398099 Array read by antidiagonals: T(n,k) is the number of inequivalent n X n symmetric nonnegative integer matrices with each row sum nonzero and at most k, up to simultaneous row and column permutations, n >= 0, k >= 0.
%C A398099 T(n,k) is the number of unlabeled multigraphs with n vertices, vertex degrees at most k, no isolated vertices and with half-edges allowed. A half-edge (also called half-loop) is a loop that adds 1 to the vertex degree.
